{"toolCallId":"call_360aa30d3d0646348c1dda1d29ec746c","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"./spec.md:92:| REQ-006 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr, so `--quiet` trims stdout only. |\n./acceptance-criteria.md:59:| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given `--quiet`, When the script writes a warning to stderr, Then that warning still appears on stderr while stdout holds only the recommendation line | `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet 2>\"$P/scratch/quiet-stderr.txt\" \\| wc -l` prints 1 and `rg -n 'QUIET' \"$S\"` shows no `2>` or `exec` stderr redirection inside `output_text()` | Unmet | - |\n./tasks.md:51:- [ ] T014 Keep the quiet branch free of stderr redirection, so every warning still reaches stderr and only stdout is trimmed (REQ-006) (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet 2>\"$P/scratch/quiet-stderr.txt\" | wc -l` prints 1 and `rg -n 'QUIET' \"$S\"` shows no `2>` or `exec` redirection inside `output_text()`.\n---\n6\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"e15095","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
